I ran into a geologist friend last night--I didn't get all of the details,
but apparently the continents are scientifically defined, in that they are
made of a specific kind of rock, and that they are not attached to other
land masses in any significant way.  So, India has the right rock, but since
it's sutured to Asia, is not a continent (although it was until it ran into
Asia).

I still kind of like the idea of using the plates, though--gets us the
expected continents, but also a "Middle East" and an "Indian sub-continent"
all in one go.

Chris

